    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42285" root="وكت" body-key="w">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكَتَ</span></b> , aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَكِتُ</span>, (inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكَتٌ</span>, <i>He,</i> or <i>it,
made a mark,</i> or <i>impression,</i> or <i>left a mark.</i>
(K.) You say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكَتَ شَيْئًا</span> <i>He,</i> or <i>it, made a
mark,</i> or <i>impression,</i> or <i>left a mark, upon a
thing.</i> (TK.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكَتَ</span> aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَكِتُ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكْتٌ</span>;
and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وِكّت</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوْكِيتٌ</span>; <i>He filled</i> (K.) a
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قِرْبَة</span>, (Lh,) or a cup, or the like, as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زكت</span>.
(Fr.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكَتَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَكِتُ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكْتٌ</span>, <i>He
walked,</i> or <i>went, with short steps.</i> (Sh, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<i>He</i> (a beast of carriage) <i>raised and put down
his feet quickly.</i> (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكَتَ المَشْىَ</span>, inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكْتٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكَتَانٌ</span>, <i>He went,</i> or <i>walked, with
short steps, but in a heavy and ugly manner.</i>
(L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِى سَيْرِهِ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكّت</span></b>  He went with a particular kind of pace. (L, from Kr.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكَتَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الكِتَابَ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكْتٌ</span>, <i>He pointed,</i> or <i>dotted, the
book, writing,</i> or <i>letter.</i> (L.)

